nsidered_alternatives": ["B2.2", "B1.2", "B3"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=57%, source=both]\n\nBiliary Obstruction with Complications vs Ectopic Pregnancy with Hemorrhagic Shock:\n  Favours first:  clay-colored stools, dark urine, fatigue, fever, jaundice\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity\n\nBiliary Obstruction with Complications vs Budd-Chiari Syndrome (Hepatic Vein Obstruction):\n  Favours first:  clay-colored stools, dark urine, fatigue, loss of appetite, nausea and vomiting\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, acute hepatic failure, ascites, autosomal recessive inheritance, budd-chiari syndrome\n\nBiliary Obstruction with Complications vs Portal Vein Thrombosis:\n  Favours first:  clay-colored stools, dark urine, fever, jaundice, loss of appetite\n  Favours second: abducens palsy, abnormal auditory evoked potentials, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal circulating copper concentration, abnormal cranial nerve morphology\n\nEctopic Pregnancy with Hemorrhagic Shock vs Budd-Chiari Syndrome (Hepatic Vein Obstruction):\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n  Favours second: acute hepatic failure, ascites, budd-chiari syndrome, cholecystitis, cirrhosis\n\nEctopic Pregnancy with Hemorrhagic Shock vs Portal Vein Thrombosis:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity\n  Favours second: abducens palsy, abnormal auditory evoked potentials, abnormal cerebral white matter morphology, abnormal circulating copper concentration, abnormal cranial nerve morphology\n\nBudd-Chiari Syndrome (Hepatic Vein Obstruction) vs Portal Vein Thrombosis:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, acute hepatic failure, as